    {
      "id": "Question 1",
      "title": "Continue the Jackson County anti-crime sales tax (COMBAT)",
      "summary": "This question asks whether Jackson County should continue its quarter-cent anti-crime sales tax, known as COMBAT, for ten more years. The money would pay for public safety, including drug abuse prevention and treatment and the investigation, prosecution and detention of violent criminals and drug dealers. Proceeds would go into a separate Jackson County Anti-Crime Sales Tax Trust Fund, apart from the county's general fund.",
      "yesMeans": "The one-quarter-cent COMBAT sales tax continues for ten years to fund public safety and drug abuse prevention and treatment programs.",
